  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-browser",
      "text": "Browser automation for DeepSeek Harness via [bsk](https://github.com/anthropics/browser-skill) — lets your agent navigate, snapshot, click, fill, and screenshot the **real Chromium browser** (with your logins)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin add dsh-browser\n```\n\nRequires `bsk` on PATH + the browser-skill extension loaded (see browser-skill prerequisites)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| Tool | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `browse_navigate` | Open a URL |\n| `browse_snapshot` | Read the page as an accessibility tree (with @eN refs) |\n| `browse_click` | Click an element by @eN ref or CSS selector |\n| `browse_fill` | Type into an input |\n| `browse_screenshot` | Capture a screenshot |\n| `browse_observe` | Semantic VOM observation |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Example",
      "text": "> Open https://example.com, read the page, and tell me the title."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
